    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense, boasting a team-high efficiency score of 83.29. The matchup against Grant Holmes (4.75 xERA) provides the ideal conditions for **Gunnar Henderson** to capitalize, aided by a significant +18% boost from the SP matchup and a +14% platoon edge. Joining him at the top of the projected outputs, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.88) maintains a strong floor despite a difficult matchup against Patrick Sandoval, with his performance buoyed by a +7% park factor and favorable batting order placement. While the weather remains stable, the primary concern across the board is the \"Lineup Pending\" status for almost every starter, which forces us to rely on historical order projections; should **Drake Baldwin** or **Jacob Wilson** slide down the lineup upon official confirmation, their projected value will face immediate downward pressure.\n\nStrategic emphasis on stolen bases continues to influence the roster construction, as seen in the selection of **Nasim Nunez** (64.58). While his raw projection is modest, the +4% \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus against Eduardo Rodriguez highlights our targeted approach to stealing bags in a 5x5 Roto environment. The decision to bench **Miguel Vargas** (60.12) was the most difficult of the morning; despite a strong score and a positive stolen base indicator against Spencer Arrighetti, **Miguel Vargas** ultimately fell just short of the efficiency threshold required to displace the current outfield configuration. We are also keeping a close eye on **Heliot Ramos** (66.08), who holds a unique upside today thanks to a beneficial wind-out factor and a strong matchup against Grayson Rodriguez. Owners should monitor the official lineup reports closely, as any sudden shifts could force a pivot back to our bench depth.",
